180
00:13:45,682 --> 00:13:49,595
because he was already sending in Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to lead the entire enterprise.

181
00:13:50,301 --> 00:13:55,285
 He sent a letter to Mad'oor(مذعور), telling him I take your word for it, what you said.

182
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:59,004
Even though it might have been an exaggeration of his abilities Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم).

183
00:13:59,079 --> 00:14:03,907
He said: I take your word for what you said and I believe you and I'm asking you

184
00:14:04,438 --> 00:14:09,709
to join hands with Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and to be with him and to follow him, wherever he goes.

185
00:14:10,798 --> 00:14:13,952
 Rather than put Mad'oor(مذعور) and Muthanna(مثنى) in the same.

186
00:14:14,505 --> 00:14:18,302
I mean, he could have told Mad'oor(مذعور) to go under the leadership of Muthanna(مثنى),

187
00:14:18,466 --> 00:14:23,535
 whom I already appointed, he could have done that and some complications could have came out of that situation.

188
00:14:23,718 --> 00:14:25,392
He said: No! You go with Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

189
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:26,876
So he separated between the two.

190
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:29,268
Al-Muthanna Bin Harisa(ألمثنى بن حارثه) is leading an army

191
00:14:29,608 --> 00:14:33,283
and Mad'oor(مذعور) with his group are following the leadership of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

192
00:14:34,283 --> 00:14:36,876
and nobody can contest the leadership with Khalid(خالد).

193
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:43,182
They all agree to the ability and the leadership of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

194
00:14:43,206 --> 00:14:48,028
I mean, Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who are earlier in Islam than him would all admit

195
00:14:48,628 --> 00:14:53,266
that Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه is the most capable among us, in leading Armies.

196
00:14:55,183 --> 00:14:57,262
What was the plan of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)?

197
00:14:57,303 --> 00:15:00,266
Al-Muthanna Bin Harisa(ألمثنى بن حارثه) played a role for some time.

198
00:15:01,076 --> 00:15:09,814
But now, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) wants to have a greater enterprise in the area of Iraq.

199
00:15:10,452 --> 00:15:18,329
So his plan was to send two armies, one army to attack from the south east

200
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:21,921
and the second army to attack from the northwest.

201
00:15:23,441 --> 00:15:27,396
The army that would attacked from the south east was the army of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

202
00:15:27,475 --> 00:15:31,332
 and he sent him a letter saying go on towards Iraq.

203
00:15:31,357 --> 00:15:33,928
Because Khalid(خالد) was in Al-Yamamah(أليمامة) he just finished off

204
00:15:34,467 --> 00:15:36,604
the Harb(حرب) with was Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب).

205
00:15:37,850 --> 00:15:40,611
Go on towards Iraq, until you enter it

206
00:15:40,935 --> 00:15:44,416
began with the gateway to India, which is Al-Ubullah(ألأبلَّى),

207
00:15:45,295 --> 00:15:50,683
they used to call the area of Al-Basra(ألبصرة), they used to call it the gateway to India,

208
00:15:51,347 --> 00:15:55,320
because anybody traveling to India would go through the Persian sea.

209
00:15:56,081 --> 00:16:00,726
So they would call it the gateway to India, he said: And start from the gateway to India

210
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:05,694
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) it is interesting as if Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is seeing the map in front of him.

211
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:09,337
 When there were no maps, in their hands.

212
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:14,506
He said: So you enter from the gateway to India, which is Al-Ubullah(ألأبلَّى)

213
00:16:15,479 --> 00:16:19,845
render that people of Persia and those nations under their rule peaceable.

214
00:16:21,064 --> 00:16:23,104
And then he sent an army from the northwest,

215
00:16:23,544 --> 00:16:27,697
under the leadership of Ayyad Bin Ghanam(عياض بن غنم), one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

216
00:16:28,546 --> 00:16:32,291
and he told him to attack from Al-Musayikh(ألمصيخ) which is the North West.

217
00:16:33,061 --> 00:16:36,407
And then look at this strategic sense of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

218
00:16:37,631 --> 00:16:42,069
He said: You both start attacking inwards into Iraq

219
00:16:42,646 --> 00:16:44,916
and try racing towards Al-Heira(ألحيرة)

220
00:16:45,523 --> 00:16:49,229
and whoever gets to Al-Heira(ألحيرة) first is the Ameer(أمير) over the other one.

221
00:16:49,748 --> 00:16:55,586
Al-Heira(ألحيرة) was midway between Al-Ubullah(ألأبلَّى) and Al-Musayikh(ألمصيخ).

222
00:16:56,387 --> 00:16:59,018
And Al-Heira(ألحيرة) is in a very strategic position.

223
00:17:00,419 --> 00:17:06,425
It is very close to Al-Madain(ألمدائن) which is the capital of the Persian Empire,

224
00:17:06,918 --> 00:17:09,628
but it's towards the Arabian Peninsula side.

225
00:17:10,903 --> 00:17:14,549
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted them to set base in a Al-Heira(ألحيرة).

226
00:17:14,574 --> 00:17:17,641
So, the two armies attack from the north and the south.

227
00:17:17,884 --> 00:17:19,864
They meet in Al-Heira(ألحيرة), they joined together

228
00:17:20,243 --> 00:17:26,607
and then they make their final hit at the Capital, which was a very strategic plan.

229
00:17:26,747 --> 00:17:31,054
This is his letter, he said: When you have joined each other at Al-Heira(ألحيرة),

230
00:17:31,687 --> 00:17:33,719
have broken the defenses of Persia

231
00:17:34,265 --> 00:17:37,730
and are sure that the Muslims will not be attacked from behind.

232
00:17:38,214 --> 00:17:42,227
Let one of you cover the Muslims and his comrade by staying at Al-Heira(ألحيرة).

233
00:17:42,886 --> 00:17:47,032
Let the other attack Allah's enemy and your enemy

234
00:17:47,429 --> 00:17:51,270
 in their own house and the abode of their power, Al-Madain(ألمدائن).

235
00:17:53,350 --> 00:17:57,565
Masaleh Kisra(مصالح كسرى), the army base of Kisra(كسرى) was towards the south.

236
00:17:58,248 --> 00:18:01,980
So it was the job of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to take care of the army basis,

237
00:18:02,764 --> 00:18:05,982
and Ayyad Bin Ghanam(عياض بن غنم) will come from the desert side

238
00:18:06,357 --> 00:18:09,621
and descend south, until they meet in Al-Heira(ألحيرة),

239
00:18:09,873 --> 00:18:12,792
whoever reaches Al-Heira(ألحيرة) first leads the other

240
00:18:13,181 --> 00:18:18,030
and then one of you stays behind and protects the rear of the army

241
00:18:18,901 --> 00:18:23,967
and the other should make a move towards Al-Madain(ألمدائن), the capital of the Persian Empire.

242
00:18:24,979 --> 00:18:28,634
 A word on this, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted to

243
00:18:29,489 --> 00:18:33,412
hit the capital and bring an end to the Persian Empire.

244
00:18:34,114 --> 00:18:39,680
Islam does not recognize a government that does not rule by the Hukm(حكم) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

245
00:18:40,406 --> 00:18:46,325
but Islam does allow the existence of other religions in the form of Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل الذمة).

246
00:18:47,092 --> 00:18:50,626
So there is tolerance of Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل الذمة) people following another religion,

247
00:18:51,154 --> 00:18:54,867
but the rule should belong to Allah over all the earth.

248
00:18:55,420 --> 00:19:00,820
So there's no recognition at all, in Islam to any disbelieving government.

249
00:19:01,117 --> 00:19:06,211
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) wants to hit the Persian Empire at its capital

250
00:19:06,328 --> 00:19:09,381
and bring an end to it and it was a very ambitious plan,

251
00:19:10,028 --> 00:19:14,486
especially that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has just finished off Harb Ar-Riddah(حرب الردَّة)

252
00:19:15,106 --> 00:19:17,301
and immediately he is sending out these two armies

253
00:19:17,326 --> 00:19:20,043
and he's not telling them just to take the outskirts.

254
00:19:20,262 --> 00:19:21,665
He's saying: You go straight to Al-Madain(ألمدائن).

255
00:19:23,504 --> 00:19:25,512
Now in his letter, he said;

256
00:19:26,168 --> 00:19:30,635
Render the people of Persia and those nations under their rule peaceable.

257
00:19:31,692 --> 00:19:35,025
It was a Persian Empire, not all of the people were Persian, there were some Arabs.

258
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:43,282
there were some different races because their rule covered a major part of Asia.

259
00:19:44,699 --> 00:19:47,152
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was saying;

260
00:19:47,176 --> 00:19:51,456
تعلف أهل الفارس ومن كان تحتهم من الأمم

261
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,961
Render these people peaceful, try to attract them towards Islam,

262
00:19:57,128 --> 00:20:01,186
which is a very different message than he was giving to his leaders regarding Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين),

263
00:20:02,019 --> 00:20:06,839
with Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين) he was saying: Whoever lands in your hands, finish them off.

264
00:20:07,334 --> 00:20:12,121
But here he is saying try to attract them, try to bring them close to Islam

265
00:20:12,161 --> 00:20:17,149
because the objective of this war is completely different than the objective of the wars of Riddah(ردَّة).

266
00:20:17,638 --> 00:20:22,054
The wars of Riddah(ردَّة) was intended to bring back Muslims back to the rule of Islam.

267
00:20:23,143 --> 00:20:32,250
While these are wars against people, who have not harmed the Muslims, have not conspired against them.

268
00:20:32,533 --> 00:20:36,690
So now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is getting into territories that didn't harm the Muslims.

269
00:20:36,794 --> 00:20:38,873
they didn't break any Muslim law or anything,

270
00:20:39,484 --> 00:20:41,373
 this was a war for Da'wah(دعوة)

271
00:20:41,778 --> 00:20:43,762
the purpose of it was Da'wah Ilallah(دعوة الى الله).

272
00:20:44,675 --> 00:20:47,685
So he's saying, when you get into Persia,

273
00:20:48,645 --> 00:20:53,363
try to attract the commoners to Islam, try to bring them closer to the folds of the religion.

274
00:20:53,793 --> 00:20:58,364
So you can see that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is dealing with a different standard, with Harub Ar-Riddah(حروب الردَّة)

275
00:20:58,690 --> 00:21:04,904
 and these wars of conquest which are done for the sake of Da'wah(دعوة), calling the people to Allah.

276
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:12,695
He also told the Armies call to arms those who fought against the apostates

277
00:21:12,727 --> 00:21:16,608
and those who have remained steadfast to Islam after the Prophet,

278
00:21:16,957 --> 00:21:22,988
do not let anyone who had apostasized campaign with you, until I give my opinion.

279
00:21:23,644 --> 00:21:27,786
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is giving clear instructions to his generals

280
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:33,912
that you should not allow any of the former Murtaddeen(مرتدين) to join in your armies,

281
00:21:34,295 --> 00:21:40,076
even though they're now Muslim, but they shall not fight with you.

282
00:21:41,391 --> 00:21:44,029
Why would Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه do that?

283
00:21:44,497 --> 00:21:49,759
When, he is in great need for as much reinforcements as he can.

284
00:21:50,657 --> 00:21:54,801
Allah Ho Alam(ألله أعلم) but what you could say is that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

285
00:21:54,962 --> 00:22:03,204
did not want people who have given up Islam at one point of time, join in armies

286
00:22:03,276 --> 00:22:05,926
 because maybe their intention would not be pure.

287
00:22:06,690 --> 00:22:09,576
These are wars of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

288
00:22:09,987 --> 00:22:14,114
these are not wars for booty, these are not wars for expansion

289
00:22:14,544 --> 00:22:19,821
this is not a war for pride, these are not wars to oppress others

290
00:22:20,591 --> 00:22:22,360
this is to bring the people to Islam.

291
00:22:22,817 --> 00:22:25,597
So people who have formerly given up Islam,

292
00:22:25,890 --> 00:22:28,461
how could they go out and invite the people to it?

293
00:22:28,757 --> 00:22:31,090
Even though they were Muslim today, and then he said;

294
00:22:31,130 --> 00:22:31,864
 "حتى أرَا رائ"

295
00:22:31,889 --> 00:22:37,482
Until I make a decision otherwise, so he wants to wait.

296
00:22:38,025 --> 00:22:43,442
Therefore, none of the people who participated in the Riddah(ردَّة) were allowed to join in the Muslim armies.

297
00:22:45,002 --> 00:22:49,564
To add to the complication of the situation, he sends them a letter telling them,

298
00:22:50,043 --> 00:22:51,624
ولا تستفتح بمستكرح

299
00:22:52,637 --> 00:22:54,639
And do not force anyone to go along with you.

300
00:22:55,403 --> 00:22:58,957
From the original soldiers that you had, from the people who were Muslim

301
00:22:59,279 --> 00:23:02,686
if they don't want to go along, don't force them to go along,

302
00:23:03,313 --> 00:23:09,440
because this is a voluntary war, this is not a defensive war, this is an offensive war.

303
00:23:10,087 --> 00:23:12,426
Therefore, it is what is called Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب).

304
00:23:12,610 --> 00:23:14,096
There is Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب), and Jihad Ad-Dafah(جهادألدفع).

305
00:23:14,370 --> 00:23:17,381
Jihad Ad-Dafah(جهادألدفع) is when you're defending yourself, this is Fard Aein(فرض عين) on everyone.

306
00:23:17,899 --> 00:23:22,855
But now this Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب) you're attacking somebody else's land,

307
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,836
therefore it's voluntary, it's not Fard Aein(فرض عين)

308
00:23:26,256 --> 00:23:27,454
it's Fard Kifayah(فرض كفاية).

309
00:23:27,692 --> 00:23:30,803
So he told his leaders do not force anyone to go along with you.

310
00:23:31,283 --> 00:23:36,573
So no Murtaddeen(مرتدين) and don't force the Muslims to go, made it difficult.

311
00:23:37,134 --> 00:23:44,445
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه saw this as being the most appropriate way to deal with this situation.

312
00:23:45,643 --> 00:23:48,022
Khalid(خالد) asked for reinforcements.

313
00:23:48,477 --> 00:23:52,702
I mean, some of his forces are deserting him.

314
00:23:53,143 --> 00:23:57,269
They're exhausted because of one battle after another, I mean,

315
00:23:57,353 --> 00:23:59,236
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was described as

316
00:23:59,261 --> 00:24:01,139
لا ينام ولا يترك أحد ينام

317
00:24:02,144 --> 00:24:04,750
He would not sleep and not allow anybody to sleep

318
00:24:06,051 --> 00:24:08,751
Friend or Foe, he could keep everyone busy.

319
00:24:09,276 --> 00:24:15,735
I mean, if you look at the record of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he's jumping from one battle to another within days.

320
00:24:16,269 --> 00:24:20,092
He's going on from one place to another all over like a tornado.

321
00:24:20,965 --> 00:24:24,750
So obviously, some of his soldiers are having a hard time keeping up with him.

322
00:24:25,425 --> 00:24:29,320
So they start to deserting him, so he's asking for reinforcements.

323
00:24:30,131 --> 00:24:31,487
Who can Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) send?

324
00:24:32,241 --> 00:24:36,541
He doesn't want to force people to go, he doesn't want to allow the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) to join.

325
00:24:36,972 --> 00:24:39,972
So he sends him Al-Qa'Qaa Bin Amr(ألقعقاع بن عمرو), one man.

326
00:24:40,675 --> 00:24:42,156
So, the Khalifah(خليفه) was told.

327
00:24:43,311 --> 00:24:48,157
Are you reinforcing a man who's troops have deserted him, with only one man?

328
00:24:48,515 --> 00:24:50,468
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

329
00:24:50,539 --> 00:24:53,905
 An army in which there is the like of this man, will not be defeated?

330
00:24:55,059 --> 00:24:59,449
If Al-Qa'Qaa(ألقعقاع) is in an army, don't worry, that army would not lose.

331
00:25:00,106 --> 00:25:04,922
So he sends one man as reinforcement to Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه.

332
00:25:06,352 --> 00:25:14,120
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) gets into Iraq, and he's appointed the general Ameer(أمير) of all of the forces.

333
00:25:14,644 --> 00:25:18,536
 So now he has under him 18,000 troops.

334
00:25:19,454 --> 00:25:27,198
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he sends a message and this was the Sunnah(سنة) of our generals,

335
00:25:27,509 --> 00:25:30,969
before war, they would send a letter giving Da'wah(دعوة) to the people.

336
00:25:31,351 --> 00:25:37,281
So he sent a letter to Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان), who was in the area of Al-Ubullah(ألأبلَّى),

337
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:39,434
which is very close to Al-Basra(ألبصرى).

338
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:43,806
He says: I call you to Allah and to Islam.

339
00:25:44,362 --> 00:25:47,735
If you respond to the call, then you are Muslims.

340
00:25:47,955 --> 00:25:53,867
You obtain the benefits they enjoy, and take up the responsibilities, they bear.

341
00:25:54,445 --> 00:25:57,639
If you refuse, then you must pay Jizya(جزية),

342
00:25:58,226 --> 00:26:02,568
if you refuse the Jizya(جزية) I will bring against you tribes of people

343
00:26:02,782 --> 00:26:06,011
who are more eager for death than you are for life.

344
00:26:06,644 --> 00:26:10,242
We will then fight you until Allah decides between us and you.

345
00:26:10,582 --> 00:26:16,561
Very decisive, clear, to the point, no confusion whatsoever, he sends this letter,

346
00:26:16,811 --> 00:26:19,115
Al-Hurmozan(ألهرمزان) refuses and he decides to fight

347
00:26:19,256 --> 00:26:25,301
so they go out to the battlefield and it was called Marakah Tis-Salasil(معركة السلاسل), the Battle of the chains.

348
00:26:25,777 --> 00:26:32,764
Because the enemy, the heart is so weak, they have to tie themselves to each other in chains.

349
00:26:33,146 --> 00:26:34,256
So, that they wouldn't run away.

350
00:26:35,412 --> 00:26:41,835
While the Muslims are so eager to die, you want the chain to bring them back, to slow them down.

351
00:26:42,534 --> 00:26:46,052
 And these are having chains so that they wouldn't run away.

352
00:26:47,169 --> 00:26:51,503
It was a disastrous defeat for the enemy.

353
00:26:52,397 --> 00:26:56,835
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) immediately moves on to Al-Mazar(ألمضار), another defeat to the enemy,

354
00:26:57,034 --> 00:26:57,839
 Al-Walajah(ألولجة).

355
00:26:58,586 --> 00:27:02,457
When he gets to Al-Walajah(ألولجة) now he's getting into the beautiful places of Iraq

356
00:27:02,481 --> 00:27:05,248
in terms of the farmland and the produce.

357
00:27:06,092 --> 00:27:09,718
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) he gave a Khut'ba(خطبة) to his troops before the battle.

358
00:27:10,402 --> 00:27:14,814
He said: Can't you see all of the produce of this land?

359
00:27:16,029 --> 00:27:21,658
By Allah! It struggled for Allah's sake, if Jihad(جهاد) for Allah's sake

360
00:27:21,682 --> 00:27:25,201
and calling the people to Islam were not required of us,

361
00:27:25,705 --> 00:27:28,631
and there were no consideration except our livelihood.

362
00:27:28,987 --> 00:27:33,667
The wise opinion would still have been that we strike this countryside, until we possess it.

363
00:27:34,518 --> 00:27:39,272
And that we leave hunger and decrease whoever stayed behind and didn't join you.

364
00:27:39,902 --> 00:27:42,270
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is looking at this blessed land.

365
00:27:42,598 --> 00:27:47,213
He is saying: If Jihad(جهاد) was not a duty on us, and Da'wah(دعوة) is not a duty on us,

366
00:27:47,608 --> 00:27:52,822
just the beauty of this land and the wealth of it, is sufficient enough as a reason to invite us to come here.

